 "figures": {
  "effects": {
   "title": "What each switch does, among the sixteen and alone",
   "caption": "Orange: each switch's main effect among the sixteen worlds of batch U \u2014 the mean of the eight worlds with it on, minus the mean of the eight with it off \u2014 at iteration 1,000. Grey: the same switch thrown alone in B2, the world with it minus its twin without it, seeds 1 and 2. The grey band round zero is the seed's own noise: one standard deviation of the measure over the lab's ten B2 worlds, twice the noise of a main effect.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Batch U's sixteen pilot worlds (`GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/U/`): B2 at 10,000 tokens, seed 1, 1,000 iterations, with each of eight switches on in eight of them (`research/oee/pilots/make_jobs_TU.py`); each switch alone in B2, seeds 1 and 2, from the batch or lab experiment that made it; and the lab's ten B2 worlds (Experiment 16) for the seed's own noise.\n\n**Data.** From each world's checkpoint at iteration 1,000, or the lab's whole world kept then (`research/atlas/at.py --at 1000`, `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/atlas/at1000.json`).\n\n1. Read each world as `research/atlas/profile.py` reads every world.\n2. A switch's main effect: the mean of the eight worlds with it on, minus the mean of the eight with it off.\n3. Thrown alone: the world with the switch minus its twin without it, each seed.\n4. The seed noise: the standard deviation of the lab's ten B2 worlds at iteration 1,000.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py eightswitches`."
  },
  "pairs": {
   "title": "Switches that act together",
   "caption": "The seven chains of pairs of batch U (book/notes/fractional-factorial.md): for each, the mean of the eight worlds where the product of the pair's two switches is +1, minus the mean of the other eight \u2014 the sum of the four pairs' effects that one chain cannot tell apart. The grey band: the seed's own noise, as in the figure above.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Batch U's sixteen pilot worlds (`GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/U/`): B2 at 10,000 tokens, seed 1, 1,000 iterations, with each of eight switches on in eight of them (`research/oee/pilots/make_jobs_TU.py`); each switch alone in B2, seeds 1 and 2, from the batch or lab experiment that made it; and the lab's ten B2 worlds (Experiment 16) for the seed's own noise.\n\n**Data.** From each world's checkpoint at iteration 1,000, or the lab's whole world kept then (`research/atlas/at.py --at 1000`, `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/atlas/at1000.json`).\n\n1. Read each world as `research/atlas/profile.py` reads every world.\n2. A chain's effect: the mean of the eight worlds where the product of a pair's switches is +1, minus the mean of the other eight.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py eightswitches`."
  },
  "evolution": {
   "title": "Do the brains of 1,000 beat those of 500?",
   "caption": "Above: each world of batch U, the share of a contested world its brains of iteration 1,000 hold after 100 iterations against those of 500, the mean of two contests, one in each era's world; the dashed line marked B2 is the median of the lab's ten B2 worlds, played the same way. Below: each switch's main effect on that share; the grey band is the spread of the ten B2 worlds (one standard deviation), twice the noise of a main effect.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Batch U's sixteen pilot worlds (`GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/U/`): B2 at 10,000 tokens, seed 1, 1,000 iterations, with each of eight switches on in eight of them (`research/oee/pilots/make_jobs_TU.py`); each switch alone in B2, seeds 1 and 2, from the batch or lab experiment that made it; and the lab's ten B2 worlds (Experiment 16) for the seed's own noise.\n\n**Data.** From `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/batch_TUV_T100.json` and, for B2, `long_steps.json` (`research/oee/checks/rejudge.py`).\n\n1. Seat the brains of the two eras on alternate agents of each era's world and play 100 iterations.\n2. Count the agents the later era's brains hold, as a share of all.\n3. A switch's main effect: the mean of the eight worlds with it on, minus the other eight.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py eightswitches`."
  }
 }
}
